,"signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787428172843023001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Symptom (observed 2026-08-22 ~19:35-19:50 UTC, main checkout + worktrees at ~af3ea35617f)\n\nUnder heavy multi-session load (~20 concurrent rebar CLI processes across worktrees sharing\nthe one tracker), `rebar show airborne-wellloved-kingfisher` (epic 2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a,\n23 children) produced ZERO output for >200 s across two attempts (killed at 75 s and 211 s).\nMeanwhile, in the same window, on the same store:\n\n- `rebar list --parent 2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a` — a strictly LARGER payload (778.6 KB, all 23\n  children serialized) — completed in ~67 s.\n- Other rebar writes (comment/edit/link/claim) completed in 3-30 s.\n- EVERY rebar invocation logs `WARNING rebar.llm.enrich_drain: enrich drain gate check took\n  N ms (> 20 ms budget)` with N observed 339-3589 ms (17-180x budget).\n\n## Why this looks like a defect, not just load\n\nThe asymmetry is the signal: `show` (one ticket + children summaries) stalls indefinitely\nwhile `list --parent` (full serialization of the same subtree) completes. That suggests\n`show` takes a path with per-child store reads, lock acquisition, or enrich-drain gate checks\nthat serialize/contend quadratically, rather than the bulk read `list` uses. The enrich-drain\noverruns being universal suggests the gate check itself does store reads under contention.\n\n## Repro guidance (load-dependent; account for non-determinism)\n\nNeeds concurrent-writer pressure: run N>=10 parallel rebar processes (mix of comment/edit/\ntransition) against one store while timing `rebar show <epic-with-20+-children>` vs\n`rebar list --parent <same>`. Quantify the stall rate; a single fast run does not reject.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause confirmed via /rebar-debug (mechanism named at file:line, discriminating\n      experiment run, caused_by attributed).\n- [ ] `rebar show <epic>` completes within the same order of magnitude as\n      `rebar list --parent <epic>` under the repro's concurrent load.\n- [ ] The enrich-drain gate-check overrun is either fixed or its budget/warning recalibrated\n      with a recorded rationale (no silent 180x-over-budget steady state).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c6270e27-222c-4341-ad33-9179b504c384","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3d57-602f-0b75-48ee","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar show stalls indefinitely on an epic under concurrent store load while list --parent completes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5561f7aa-15dd-4bd3-8f71-cc707153db55","c6270e27-222c-4341-ad33-9179b504c384","edc7a1e4-2f8d-43a1-b762-e35e69a2ec97"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787430614135280001,"uuid":"4e92b5cf-9b28-4f93-97a3-36313f68cb47"}